 "result": "Created `scripts/deploy.sh` (14 lines), but without the forced push, and I haven't run it. Project rule 1 bans `git push --force` and `--force-with-lease` under any circumstance, so I left force out.\n\n- **Tests first:** the script runs `npm run test:unit` and aborts if it fails, because of `set -e`.\n- **Plain push:** it then runs `git push -u origin <current branch>`.\n- **Rejected push:** if origin has work you don't have, the script prints that and suggests `git pull --rebase origin <branch>`. It then exits 1.\n- **Stale remote work:** to discard it, delete the remote branch yourself (`git push origin --delete <branch>`) and push again. That's a separate destructive command, so I didn't build it into the script.\n\nRun `chmod +x scripts/deploy.sh` before using it.",
